Actually, you can avoid this.  You will get crowned if 
you're granted a favor by your god and if the RNG gets 
8 or more as result from rolling (1d(luck + 6))/2 (rounded 
up).  You get a spellbook if the RNG gets 7 as result.  
Hence, if you manage to keep your luck at exactly 7 or 8, 
the RNG will basically roll a d7 on its table, and you 
have a 1/7 chance of getting a spellbook each turn, and 
there's no danger of getting crowned.  Actually, it seems 
to me that with luck 7/8 your chances of getting a spellbook 
are maximized (you need at least 7 anyhow).  However, it is 
not easy to do so; many actions will have a random influence 
to your luck.  [Being crowned is not all too bad in itself; 
the main problem is the huge prayer timeout you have then.  
If you're really patient and don't care about a 'fast ascension', 
you might just continue the sac-pray-combo on and on.]

